  "title": "A day in the life of an accountant: accruals",
  "slug": "life-of-accountant",
  "family_or_category": "accounting",
  "caption": "Month-end is when accountants make sure every cost lands in the right month\n\nThe October electricity bill arrives on 3 November. It still belongs to October, because that is when the power was used. That is an accrual: you record a cost when it happens, not when the cash moves\n\nSave this for your next month-end close\n\n#edlintics #businessstudents #accounting #finance",
  "caption_x": "A day in the life of an accountant: the October bill arrives in November, and it still belongs to October. That is an accrual. edlintics.com #edlintics",
  "first_comment": "Which month-end task takes you the longest? Reply below. Bonus question: a shop pays its December rent of $3,000 on 2 January. In which month does the rent expense belong? Reply with the month",
  "maths_check": "Bonus: December. The rent is for December, so the expense is recorded in December (an accrued expense), even though the cash leaves in January.",
